= Validation set — Technical =

== Selection role ==
For candidate systems h_1,...,h_k and validation criterion C:

<pre>
h* = argmin_h C(h, S_val)
</pre>

The selected h* is statistically dependent on S_val even if its fitted parameters were learned only from S_train.

== Selection bias ==
When C is noisy and many candidates are searched, the extremal selected estimate is optimistically biased.

This is model-selection overfitting.

== Nested evaluation ==
Nested cross-validation separates:

<pre>
inner folds → model/hyperparameter selection
outer folds → performance estimation
</pre>

to reduce leakage between selection and evaluation roles.

